 # H7 fixture · locale trap
 
-A web plugin whose browser half locates the host session-header button by
-matching the display text `/session\s*log/i`. The host client copy has been
-fully localized (rollup R-13), so the selector silently stops matching on
-non-English locales — the injected badge disappears with no error and no
-console exception. The trap comment suggests adding a second regex. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+A web plugin (host half `index.js`, browser half `client.js`, mounted by
+`cordis.patch.yml` through `dsh.bundle.patch`) whose browser half adds a `loc`
+badge to the host Session header utilities row, beside the shipped Session log
+action.
+
+The badge is a list entry in the official
+`conversation.session.header.utilities` slot (`id: bench-locale-badge`,
+`order: 1`), so it is placed by slot id and order. Host copy is fully localized
+(rollup R-13): display text is not an identity, so the plugin does not match
+button copy, and a second regex for the Chinese variant is not a fix.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
